-- title:
--   Regularity of g dJ from ord(g⁶J⁴(J-1728)³)≥ 0
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ and $F$ be fields with $F$ a $K$-algebra, and let $v$ be a place of $F$ over $K$, i.e. a valuation subring of $F$ containing the image of $K$, distinct from $F$ itself, and a principal ideal ring; write $\mathrm{ord}_v$ for the associated integer-valued order function, the negative logarithm of the adic valuation attached to the height-one prime of that subring. Assume $K$ is perfect, and let $x \in F$ be such that $F$ is finite-dimensional over the intermediate field $K(x)$ generated by $x$. For a Kähler differential $\omega \in \Omega[F/K]$, $\mathrm{ordDiff}_v(\omega)$ is defined as $\mathrm{ord}_v$ of the coefficient $h$ in a representation $\omega = h \cdot D_{K/F}(t)$, for $t$ a chosen element with $\mathrm{ord}_v(t) = 1$ (both choices being made by definite description, with value $0$ when no such element exists). Let $g, J \in F$, assume $1728 \neq 0$ in $K$ and that $0 \le \mathrm{ord}_v\bigl(g^6 J^4 (J - 1728)^3\bigr)$, the constant $1728$ being taken in $F$ via the structure map. Then $0 \le \mathrm{ordDiff}_v\bigl(g \cdot D_{K/F}(J)\bigr)$.
--
--   This is the local ceiling estimate expressing that $dJ$ is controlled at each place of a one-variable function field by the orders of $J$ and of $J - 1728$ with weights $4/6$ and $3/6$ — the classical pattern of the divisor of $dj$ on a modular curve, reflecting the ramification of the $j$-map above $j = 0$, $j = 1728$ and the cusp. It is used in the treatment of regular differentials on modular curves, notably in the identification of regular differentials through their $q$-expansions.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_Place_ordDiff_smul_D_nonneg_of_ord_pow_six_mul_pow_four_mul_sub_1728_pow_three_nonneg.lean

